{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(f) =$", "MATH_0002": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descending-property-separated}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:365d02bf050f12ee9903b36c61bdf624d00b07c1586052591e25ad225aaf043e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8ebbbaa54f3dd7e67ae2da7a3c3f27ce0e085b272949e4e806f4707f72cf8747", "source_text": "The property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is separated''\nis fpqc local on the base.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:67a2deef12a074d6e15076cc4706a83a95ac984ec456009b1830e649b6a30f42", "unit_id": "tag:02KU:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$f' : X' \\to S'$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Delta' : X' \\to X'\\times_{S'} X'$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Delta'$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Delta : X \\to X \\times_S X$", "MATH_0007": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Delta$", "MATH_0009": "$\\Delta$", "MATH_0010": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-separated-permanence}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-characterize-separated}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-universally-closed}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-diagonal-immersion}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties-morphisms}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b9061442cb5ccfe5dcd85d7a8ae7ab6ed61b0f97e850fe4dfacfed76e56c45bf", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c37d59ccd03ddce2242023ba27014bfe938e2749dd0811c03c29338c36641b1b", "source_text": "A base change of a separated morphism is separated, see\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nBeing separated is Zariski local on the base (from the\ndefinition or by\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0002>).\nFinally, let\n<MATH_0001> be a flat surjective morphism of affine schemes,\nand let <MATH_0002> be a morphism. Assume that the base change\n<MATH_0003> is separated. This means that\n<MATH_0004> is a closed immersion,\nhence universally closed.\nNote that <MATH_0005> is the base change of <MATH_0006>\nvia <MATH_0007>. By Lemma <REF_0003>\nthis implies <MATH_0008> is universally closed. Since it is\nan immersion\n(Schemes, Lemma <REF_0004>)\nwe conclude <MATH_0009> is a closed immersion.\nHence <MATH_0010> is separated.\nTherefore Lemma <REF_0005> applies and we win.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b46c2fae2f849638993eec02d300dd6866ce26813b8cb0e7f4ef12a13d6ed6c9", "unit_id": "tag:02KU:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(f) =$", "MATH_0002": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descending-property-surjective}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:365d02bf050f12ee9903b36c61bdf624d00b07c1586052591e25ad225aaf043e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:658c1792bcf151629f6d40b61f57edf64b2e04bdfb153679a128b714e7aecead", "source_text": "The property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is surjective''\nis fpqc local on the base.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:10547d83f770e92fcb38d57d6cd1687c7cf0ab3e638aec5f03c2d200d7845dac", "unit_id": "tag:02KV:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8fc055aea5a228a1a80cc6146a8f333e6d6d3e005829014d167de4951336f0e2", "source_text": "This is clear.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:30bb4c9d34db5dd6c994c5188e4cb811c587d05e7905655466b4e6c26bf63d0e", "unit_id": "tag:02KV:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(f) =$", "MATH_0002": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descending-property-dominant}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:365d02bf050f12ee9903b36c61bdf624d00b07c1586052591e25ad225aaf043e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9137829834a99f638c8a79fc30b9eea69c8235f21e8a2d1d0f6bf59b0b824333", "source_text": "The property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is quasi-compact and dominant''\nis fpqc local on the base.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bf7ee72eff161874c2957ee7d5660e57ca36b9ada2e97015296bd61b8b414f27", "unit_id": "tag:0H8H:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$f' : X' \\to S'$", "MATH_0004": "$X' \\to S'\\to S$", "MATH_0005": "$X' \\to X \\to S$", "MATH_0006": "$X\\to S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-base-change-dominant}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-quasi-compact}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f3772391b85f36bf170ab81d5dd36a4da08e13a28c779ad31cc8006439a37cb7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e4ad31ee6dbd09f084a704eb802ae1500cdbf56a8a487d4ef6ef4db1e43ca141", "source_text": "By Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>,\nquasi-compact dominant morphisms are preserved\nby flat pullback. The other direction is easier.\nIndeed, quasi-compactness is fpqc local on the base\nby Lemma <REF_0002>.\nBeing dominant is clearly Zariski local on the base.\nFinally, let <MATH_0001> be a surjective morphism of schemes\n(not necessarily flat),\nand let <MATH_0002> be a morphism. Assume that the base change\n<MATH_0003> is dominant. Then <MATH_0004> is a composite\nof two dominant morphisms, hence dominant. Since this is also\nthe composite <MATH_0005>, it follows that <MATH_0006> is dominant.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7625b8ba6c78da67d6412db93c424dd936fd89c82d5df0f583f65597af44c110", "unit_id": "tag:0H8H:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-descending-fppf-property-dominant}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:de05708efb7feed90b9b4a4e4c0582be3102ade39b61819164be5ef2a7a55402", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nDominant morphisms are not preserved by flat pullback in full generality,\nbut the following special case is worth mentioning.\nSee also Lemma <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:68f060be723fefb84b7f0ccc27c86f3df6cf0526819203d3a820caf9f8357bc8", "unit_id": "tag:02YJ:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$E/k$", "MATH_0002": "$X \\to Y$", "MATH_0003": "$k$", "MATH_0004": "$X_E \\to Y_E$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descending-property-dominant-over-field}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fba7a2c2462e168a4129af33d6b4f83c33c8aca7cb05f8000da8cad7b50f5ba5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3b58e4c1e3748a637be6745e96c02f2e0dde99f4f88e85bfd10b2843409990ce", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a field extension. Then a morphism\n<MATH_0002> over <MATH_0003> is dominant if and only if\nthe pullback <MATH_0004> is dominant.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:984c0bc1dee322c895922ceddf42ad4cfb4bb35c063261aea3cbce0aea8a0fe5", "unit_id": "tag:0H8I:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Spec(E) \\to \\Spec(k)$", "MATH_0002": "$Y_E \\to Y$", "MATH_0003": "$X \\to Y$", "MATH_0004": "$X_E \\to Y_E$", "MATH_0005": "$X_E \\to Y_E$", "MATH_0006": "$Y_E \\to Y$", "MATH_0007": "$X_E \\to Y_E \\to Y$", "MATH_0008": "$X_E \\to X \\to Y$", "MATH_0009": "$X \\to Y$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-scheme-over-field-universally-open}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-open-base-change-dominant}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-base-change-surjective}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:772173077fff1b87d43740dc6085f29bcdeffd7e060a1880ec386a3fad0353d7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:367a714b24f6fe947a8bc3bcc58530db9023b688b15a72eb55a369fc3c5b63a4", "source_text": "By Morphisms,\nLemma <REF_0001>,\nthe morphism <MATH_0001>\nis universally open. So <MATH_0002> is open.\nTherefore, if <MATH_0003> is dominant, Morphisms,\nLemma <REF_0002> gives that\n<MATH_0004> is dominant.\nConversely, suppose that <MATH_0005> is dominant.\nThe morphism <MATH_0006> is surjective by Morphisms,\nLemma <REF_0003>, and so the composition\n<MATH_0007> is dominant. This is also the composition\n<MATH_0008>, and so <MATH_0009> is dominant.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7ffb9a8e4957acd74050b5f2ebb59798ea506156cd35395e331444ada81db266", "unit_id": "tag:0H8I:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(f) =$", "MATH_0002": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descending-property-universally-injective}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:365d02bf050f12ee9903b36c61bdf624d00b07c1586052591e25ad225aaf043e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:be5c52ee0b7839c42c45168bec40f073670c3d575f34f735aad9233722a6524e", "source_text": "The property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is universally injective''\nis fpqc local on the base.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ac878d77054671e9157c4858a4ad09b12e7dfb376e2b92f712b2b7b4e32ff634", "unit_id": "tag:02KW:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$f' : X' \\to S'$", "MATH_0004": "$K$", "MATH_0005": "$a, b : \\Spec(K) \\to X$", "MATH_0006": "$f \\circ a = f \\circ b$", "MATH_0007": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0008": "$K'/K$", "MATH_0009": "$\\Spec(K')\n\\to S'$", "MATH_0010": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Spec(K') \\ar[rrd] \\ar@{-->}[rd]_{a', b'} \\ar[dd] \\\\\n &\nX' \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\nS' \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\Spec(K) \\ar[r]^{a, b} &\nX \\ar[r] &\nS\n}\n$$", "MATH_0011": "$a'$", "MATH_0012": "$b'$", "MATH_0013": "$X' \\to S'$", "MATH_0014": "$a' = b'$", "MATH_0015": "$a = b$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-section-points}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-universally-injective}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{schemes-section-points}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties-morphisms}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-universally-injective}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-surjective}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:edee5f71fe705739b6df6051bffec750f29de51ffb692aaadacc781b7f299586", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c30e15b97e472d483401e6a1909d6338a42c1fd38e3b63fa68e03ff484d64fbe", "source_text": "A base change of a universally injective morphism is universally\ninjective (this is formal). Being universally injective is Zariski\nlocal on the base; this is clear from the definition.\nFinally, let\n<MATH_0001> be a flat surjective morphism of affine schemes,\nand let <MATH_0002> be a morphism. Assume that the base change\n<MATH_0003> is universally injective. Let <MATH_0004> be a field, and let\n<MATH_0005> be two morphisms such that\n<MATH_0006>. As <MATH_0007> is surjective and\nby the discussion in Schemes,\nSection <REF_0001> there exists a field\nextension <MATH_0008> and a morphism <MATH_0009> such that the following solid diagram commutes\n<MATH_0010>\nAs the square is cartesian we get the two dotted arrows <MATH_0011>, <MATH_0012> making the\ndiagram commute. Since <MATH_0013> is universally injective we get <MATH_0014>,\nby\nMorphisms, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nClearly this forces <MATH_0015> (by the discussion in Schemes,\nSection <REF_0003>).\nTherefore Lemma <REF_0004> applies and we win.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nAn alternative proof would be to use the characterization of a universally\ninjective morphism as one whose diagonal is surjective, see\nMorphisms, Lemma <REF_0005>.\nThe lemma then follows from the fact that\nthe property of being surjective is fpqc local on the base, see\nLemma <REF_0006>.\n(Hint: use that the base change of the diagonal is the diagonal\nof the base change.)\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:88948868195de2647b0beb6685e07a6fcc92a4c68eead97bb27c5990f032d3a5", "unit_id": "tag:02KW:proof"}
